nts right so we  talked about events before we talked  about how the um  producer can choose which events to to  to send which kind of messages to send  on  on the other side the consumers will  pick it up if they wanted to right so um  here is reddit itself acting as a  consumer sending specific specific  events around keys so  events such as delete update or expire  that means if we update a key we can get  notified if we updated a key means  updating a data a value on the storage  uh deleting a key or creating a new key  even uh means saving saving something  new to redis and we get notified  um  in particular the one i'm gonna be also  covering is the expirement which is my  favorite event because it allows you to  um it not only allows you it  completely simplifies uh the  uh the creation of time-based events so  we're gonna be covering that in a second  so but before and to highlight this um  um  you can think of  uh  microservices in a reactive architecture  as independent building blocks or lego  bricks if you will uh on the  and to put an example a very silly and  trivial example look at the site  box on on your screen so we have very  simple save user  function  that will do two things  it will save the user to uh whatever  storage we're using right and it'll  notify um  not notify sorry it'll uh send a welcome  email to that user essentially right  welcome to our application or whatever  um  the code is fine it works but there is a  slight coupling here  because  our function that is in charge of saving  the user into storage medium  is also in charge of sending an email  and that's not something that we want uh  and even if we were to abstract that  send email method into an emotional  notify or welcome user right  uh  the save user function would still be in  charge of orchestrating  uh that logic and here is again the  orchestration um  i said it before  we don't want that in our code as much  as we can because changes in that  orchestration means chan